<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="051" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Ask Legal assistant (bounded: policy_search + launch_wizard; workforce-plane app-only; no file ingest)</title>
    <phase>P5 Collaboration Surfaces</phase>
    <gate>blocked-until:050,012,034</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>AI on the external plane, app-only (no OBO), security-critical (tags bff-api/auth/frontend); implements the task-050 security design; a scope-trim omission = cross-user data leak.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>App-only AI grounding with server-side entitlement security-trim + closed tool catalog on the external plane — high-blast-radius security reasoning per CLAUDE.md §8.5.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Adds an AI endpoint group to the shared BFF AI surface + mounts the assistant pane on the shell; gated by 050 sign-off; /conflict-check required.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>050,012,034</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, frontend</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-8 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Build the "Ask Legal" assistant per the task-050 signed-off security design: a NEW workforce-plane, entitlement-scoped,
    APP-ONLY (no OBO) assistant endpoint exposing an ADR-039 closed tool catalog of EXACTLY TWO tools — policy_search (RAG
    over the task-034 P&amp;P policy index, entitlement/status-trimmed) and launch_wizard (route to a defined wizard via the
    surface-launch spine). Mount the shared context-agnostic SprkChat as the dockable assistant pane (workforce users only,
    not outside-counsel). The chat composer is TEXT-ONLY — there is NO file-upload / attach / drop affordance at all.
    Do NOT proceed unless task 050 is signed off.
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer + BFF AI engineer + Fluent v9 frontend engineer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in app-only AI grounding, ADR-039 closed tool catalogs, RAG security-trim, and mounting the context-agnostic SprkChat with pluggable auth.</role>

  <goal>
    A working Ask Legal assistant: (1) a NEW workforce-plane, entitlement-scoped, app-only BFF endpoint group with an
    ADR-039 closed catalog of exactly two tools (policy_search RAG-grounded on the P&amp;P index with server-side
    entitlement/status trim; launch_wizard routing only to defined wizards); (2) SprkChat mounted as the dockable assistant
    pane on the workspace shell for workforce users only, composer text-only (no upload affordance). All enforcement is
    server-side per the task-050 design; negative "no cross-scope leakage" tests pass per tool + for grounding; publish ≤60 MB.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Per spec FR-26 (refined 2026-08-06) + NFR-EXT-AI + design.md §12(B). Ask Legal does EXACTLY TWO things: policy_search
      (RAG over the P&amp;P library — instant, non-authoritative) + launch_wizard (surface-launch to a defined wizard: NDA /
      Policy Question / Invention / Trademark / etc.). EXPLICITLY EXCLUDED: no upload→summarize/analyze, no data queries beyond
      P&amp;P, no file-ingest tool; file analysis lives ONLY inside wizards. UI: the composer is text-only — NO paperclip / drop
      zone (removing the ingest surface is itself a security control). Workforce-internal only (single-scheme, NOT CIAM dual-scheme);
      NOT shown to external/outside-counsel. App-only RAG grounding (no OBO RetrievePrincipalAccess); the core /api/ai/chat is
      OBO/core-user and unusable. This task IMPLEMENTS the task-050 signed-off design (grounding trim, tool-catalog escape-proof,
      launch_wizard routing safety, per-tool authz, audit). Reuse: SprkChat (context-agnostic, pluggable auth), ADR-039
      AgentToolCatalogProjector (external two-tool projection), ChatKnowledgeScope, sprk_aipersona persona prompt, the task-034
      P&amp;P AI Search policy index + its governance-state trim fields, the surface-launch spine (ASSISTANT-SURFACE-LAUNCH-MECHANISM.md),
      CallerPrincipalResolver (workforce plane Tier-1/Tier-2), and the widget/pane shell from task 012.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SprkChat/</file>
      <file>src/client/external-spa/</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerPrincipalResolver.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Authentication/AuthPolicies.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Models/Ai/KnowledgeDocument.cs</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/ASSISTANT-SURFACE-LAUNCH-MECHANISM.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/external-assistant-security-design.md</file>
      <file>tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>050 (the signed-off security design this task implements — MUST be signed off first); 012 (widget registry + tabbed workspace + dockable assistant pane the SprkChat mounts into); 034 (P&amp;P document architecture — the AI Search policy index + governance-state trim fields policy_search grounds on).</dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Do NOT start until task 050 (security spike) is human-signed-off; implement the design in notes/external-assistant-security-design.md exactly — grounding trim, two-tool catalog, launch_wizard routing safety, per-tool authz, audit.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-EXT-AI">Enforcement is SERVER-SIDE (tool catalog + grounding security-trim + per-tool authz), NOT prompt-based. The assistant MUST NOT ground on or return content outside the caller's Tier-1 + Tier-2 scope; a negative "no cross-scope leakage" test is required per tool + for grounding.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">The external assistant catalog is EXACTLY TWO tools (policy_search, launch_wizard) via the AgentToolCatalogProjector external projection — no core-user tools, no file-ingest tool reachable. launch_wizard routes ONLY to allow-listed defined wizards.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">Use the Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ facade; do NOT inject AI-internal types (IOpenAiClient/IPlaybookService) into the external endpoint. App-only RAG grounding — no OBO RetrievePrincipalAccess.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">§10 BFF Hygiene: state a Placement Justification in the PR for the new assistant endpoint group (cite .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md); run /conflict-check BEFORE the PR; verify publish ≤60 MB compressed (dotnet publish -c Release; report absolute + delta vs baseline); verify no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">The assistant pane uses Fluent v9 tokens, zero hex; the chat composer has NO file-upload / attach / drop affordance; the pane is dockable (left/right) and renders correctly in dark + Teams themes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The assistant is workforce-internal only — NOT rendered for external/outside-counsel (CIAM) users; the endpoint is single-scheme workforce-plane, not CIAM dual-scheme.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Add/update tests in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ (+ KEEP-path integration); the negative cross-scope-leakage tests are mandatory; no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; / DI-registration / ctor-null tests.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-components.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-008-endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-001-minimal-api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-019-problemdetails.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/ai.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/ASSISTANT-SURFACE-LAUNCH-MECHANISM.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/external-assistant-security-design.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Closed two-tool catalog" location=".claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md">Project the external catalog to exactly two tools via AgentToolCatalogProjector; the server-side projection is the security boundary, not the persona prompt.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Context-agnostic SprkChat mount" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SprkChat/">Mount SprkChat with pluggable auth into the shell's dockable assistant pane; composer text-only (no upload affordance).</pattern>
      <pattern name="Surface-launch routing" location="docs/architecture/ASSISTANT-SURFACE-LAUNCH-MECHANISM.md">launch_wizard resolves consumerType → surfaceLaunchRegistry → handleSurfaceLaunch; only defined wizards are reachable.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Confirm task 050 is human-signed-off; load notes/external-assistant-security-design.md and restate the enforcement contract this task implements. If not signed off, STOP.</step>
    <step order="2">Run /conflict-check against the shared BFF AI surface + external-access surface before editing; record the result.</step>
    <step order="3">Add the NEW workforce-plane, entitlement-scoped, app-only assistant endpoint group (single-scheme, ExternalCollaboration/workforce plane; via Services/Ai/PublicContracts facade; no AI-internal type injection; no OBO).</step>
    <step order="4">Wire the ADR-039 external tool-catalog projection to EXACTLY TWO tools: policy_search (RAG over the task-034 P&amp;P index with server-side entitlement + published/not-restricted/effective trim) + launch_wizard (allow-listed defined wizards only). No file-ingest tool, no core-user tools.</step>
    <step order="5">Implement per-tool app-only authz + the grounding security-trim exactly per the task-050 design; wire audit logging of asks/answers/tools/grounding-sources.</step>
    <step order="6">Mount SprkChat as the dockable assistant pane in the workspace shell (from task 012) for WORKFORCE users only; composer TEXT-ONLY — remove/omit any upload/attach/drop affordance; Fluent v9 tokens, zero hex.</step>
    <step order="7">Add negative tests: out-of-entitlement question → no grounded leakage; catalog excludes all core-user tools + the file-ingest tool; launch_wizard rejects an undefined wizard id; no OBO on any path; assistant not rendered for outside-counsel.</step>
    <step order="8">Run dotnet build + dotnet test (full BFF suite green); dotnet list package --vulnerable (no new HIGH CVE); dotnet publish -c Release and record compressed size + delta vs baseline.</step>
    <step order="9">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅ completed.</step>
    <step order="10">Document any deviations in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the P&amp;P RAG grounding cannot be entitlement-trimmed app-only per the task-050 spike (server-side filter cannot guarantee no cross-scope leakage), STOP and escalate — do NOT ship a grounding path that can leak out-of-entitlement content.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test/publish .NET</tool>
    <tool name="npm">Build the external-spa / shared UI</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Shell</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ (new workforce-plane app-only assistant endpoint group + two-tool catalog projection + grounding trim + audit)</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/external-spa/ (SprkChat mounted as dockable assistant pane, workforce-only, text-only composer)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ (negative cross-scope-leakage + catalog + routing tests)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a workforce SPA user, when they ask a policy question, then policy_search returns answers grounded ONLY on published/not-restricted/effective P&amp;P within the caller's Tier-1 entitlement (app-only, no OBO).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative — grounding: given an out-of-entitlement question, when policy_search runs, then NO grounded content outside the caller's Tier-1/Tier-2 scope is returned (test green).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative — catalog: the external tool catalog contains EXACTLY policy_search + launch_wizard; all core-user tools AND any file-ingest tool are absent/unreachable (test green).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative — routing: launch_wizard routes only to an allow-listed defined wizard; an undefined/injected wizard id is rejected server-side (test green).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative — UI: the chat composer renders NO file-upload / attach / drop affordance (no paperclip, no drop zone); the assistant pane is NOT rendered for external/outside-counsel users.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative — auth: no OBO on any assistant path (app-only broker only); the endpoint is single-scheme workforce-plane.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The full BFF suite is green; no new HIGH CVE; publish ≤60 MB compressed with delta reported; Placement Justification stated in PR + /conflict-check run.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <justification>
    <existing>SprkChat (context-agnostic, pluggable auth), ADR-039 AgentToolCatalogProjector (closed catalog), ChatKnowledgeScope, sprk_aipersona persona prompt, the core /api/ai/chat endpoint. grep: no workforce-plane app-only assistant endpoint exists — /api/ai/chat is OBO/core-user (unusable for the external plane).</existing>
    <extension>Partial — REUSE SprkChat + the ADR-039 catalog + grounding seams as-is; the ONLY new surface is a workforce-plane app-only endpoint group + its two-tool external projection. The core /api/ai/chat cannot be extended because it assumes an OBO core-user Dataverse identity.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the new app-only endpoint, workforce SPA users have no way to search P&amp;P or route to wizards from the portal; reusing /api/ai/chat would require an OBO core-user token the external plane does not have, and any un-trimmed grounding path would leak out-of-entitlement policy content — the exact failure NFR-EXT-AI exists to prevent.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Assistant pane renders (workforce)">
      <steps><step>Sign in as a workforce user; open the Legal Front Door; dock the assistant pane (left, then right)</step><step>Ask a policy question; trigger launch_wizard for an NDA</step></steps>
      <expected>Pane docks both sides; grounded answer renders; wizard launches; NO paperclip/upload/drop affordance in the composer; no console errors</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Not shown to outside-counsel">
      <steps><step>Sign in as an external/outside-counsel (CIAM) user; open the portal</step></steps>
      <expected>The Ask Legal assistant pane is not rendered/available</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark + Teams theme (ADR-021)">
      <steps><step>Toggle dark theme, then Teams theme, with the assistant pane open</step></steps>
      <expected>Fluent tokens adapt; zero hardcoded hex; layout intact</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <notes>
    §10 BFF-touching + AI-on-external-plane: gated by the task-050 human sign-off. Placement Justification in PR + /conflict-check
    + publish ≤60 MB. Reuse SprkChat + ADR-039 catalog + surface-launch spine; the security boundary is server-side, not the
    persona prompt. Text-only composer (no ingest surface) is itself a security control per FR-26.
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Verify task 050 sign-off first; load all &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;; follow the task-execute pre-execution checklist; run /conflict-check before the BFF PR.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
